Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-20028) Support changing replication factor
 in kafka-reassign-partitions.sh generation mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Chia-Ping Tsai (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-20028:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Support changing replication factor in kafka-reassign-partitions.sh generation mode
                 Key: KAFKA-20028
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20028
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai


Currently, the {{kafka-reassign-partitions.sh}} tool with the {{--generate}} flag strictly adheres to the existing replication factor (RF) of the topics. It does not provide an option to modify the RF during the assignment generation process. This limitation prevents users from easily changing the replication factor of a topic



