Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-20030:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Document considerations and side effects of dynamic p=
artition expansion
                 Key: KAFKA-20030
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20030
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


We should update the documentation to list important considerations when us=
ers dynamically increase the number of partitions for a topic.

Key points to include:
 # *Key Distribution Changes:* The default partitioner=E2=80=99s mapping lo=
gic (e.g., hash of the key) changes when the partition count increases, whi=
ch may affect message ordering for existing keys.

 # *Potential Data Loss with {{{}latest{}}}:* Existing consumers configured=
 with {{auto.offset.reset=3Dlatest}} might miss messages produced to the ne=
w partitions during the window between partition creation and consumer disc=
overy.

 # *Metadata Propagation Delay:* New partitions are not immediately visible=
 to producers and consumers due to metadata refresh intervals.



