Andrew Schofield resolved KAFKA-20065.
--------------------------------------
    Resolution: Fixed

> Improve tagging of code examples in javadoc
> -------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-20065
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20065
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Improvement
>          Components: clients
>            Reporter: Andrew Schofield
>            Assignee: Andrew Schofield
>            Priority: Major
>             Fix For: 4.3.0
>
>
> The code examples in the javadoc often include HTML escaping for double quotes and angle brackets. This can be avoided by tagging the code examples as code, as opposed to just preformatted. The benefit is that the code examples are much more readable in the source code, which makes them much easier for the code authors to read and get correct.



