Chia-Ping Tsai resolved KAFKA-20030.
------------------------------------
    Fix Version/s: 4.3.0
       Resolution: Fixed

> Document considerations and side effects of dynamic partition expansion
> -----------------------------------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-20030
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20030
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Improvement
>            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
>            Assignee: Lan Ding
>            Priority: Minor
>             Fix For: 4.3.0
>
>
> We should update the documentation to list important considerations when =
users dynamically increase the number of partitions for a topic.
> Key points to include:
> *Key Distribution Changes:* The default partitioner=E2=80=99s mapping log=
ic (e.g., hash of the key) changes when the partition count increases, whic=
h may affect message ordering for existing keys.
> *Potential Data Loss with {{{}latest{}}}:* Existing consumers configured =
with {{auto.offset.reset=3Dlatest}} might miss messages produced to the new=
 partitions during the window between partition creation and consumer disco=
very.
> *Metadata Propagation Delay:* New partitions are not immediately visible =
to producers and consumers due to metadata refresh intervals.



