JR10. "Cluster scalability increases when less data is required to be
stored on disks and rebalanced between brokers."
This seems to contradict a bit with what KIP-1163 says: "Start building it
from some configurable amount, e.g. 100 MiB prior to the current log end or
earliest available offset, whichever is later.".  I just want to confirm
that we plan to make data rebalancing much faster in this KIP.

JR11. Sounds good.

JR13. Since people keep asking about the "simpler" approach, it would be
useful to include in the rejected section why we chose not to pursue the
"simpler" approach like the one in KIP-1176. To me, there are two main
reasons: (1) this KIP provides more benefits (saving all cross AZ network
costs instead of just the replication part, better scalability and
durability); (2) it provides an opportunity for a cleaner long-term design
instead of retrofitting to the existing framework unnaturally.

Jun



