Hi Jun,

> JR10. "Cluster scalability increases when less data is required to be
> stored on disks and rebalanced between brokers."
> This seems to contradict a bit with what KIP-1163 says: "Start buildin=
g it
> from some configurable amount, e.g. 100 MiB prior to the current log e=
nd or
> earliest available offset, whichever is later.".  I just want to confi=
rm
> that we plan to make data rebalancing much faster in this KIP.

This 100 MiB is at the moment not a very well researched number. Probabl=
y is should be configurable per topic and the default should be smaller.=
 Generally indeed we want to make moving Diskless partitions around, add=
ing replicas, etc. much faster and less resource-consuming than classic =
topics.

> JR13. Since people keep asking about the "simpler" approach, it would =
be
> useful to include in the rejected section why we chose not to pursue t=
he
> "simpler" approach like the one in KIP-1176. To me, there are two main
> reasons: (1) this KIP provides more benefits (saving all cross AZ netw=
ork
> costs instead of just the replication part, better scalability and
> durability); (2) it provides an opportunity for a cleaner long-term de=
sign
> instead of retrofitting to the existing framework unnaturally.

Thanks, we added [1] this to the rejected alternatives in KIP-1163.

Best,
Ivan

[1] https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=3D3=
50783976#KIP1163:DisklessCore-Coordinator-lessapproaches

