Hi, Robin,

Here is my view on the "simpler" approach. First, because the focus is only
on saving cross-AZ network costs, it doesn't achieve other potential
benefits like better scalability and durability. Secondly, the "Simpler"
approach may not be that simple once we work out the details. For example,
during the discussion in kip-1176, we realized that to really save cost, we
need to rethink how replicas are assigned to brokers to avoid different
followers reading the same object hundreds of times. Thirdly, most variants
of the "simpler" approach are unnatural. They all try to piggyback the
existing fetch request protocol desgined for data to propagate just the
metadata. This could make evolving the protocol harder in the future. With
KIP-1150, I hope that we can gain more benefits from a cleaner design
that's more maintainable for the long term.

Hi, Ivan,

Thanks for the updated KIP. LGTM now.

Jun



