Hi Andrew,

I want to apologize: somehow we forgot to transfer the section on cluste=
r metadata from our draft document to the wiki. Now it's added [1]

I hope it may answer AS1 and AS2. Effectively the idea is the following:
1. If the MetadataRequest is of the new version and contains RackId, no =
lying: we tell the real leader, the replicas, the preferred produce brok=
ers and IsDiskless flag to inform the client and let it decide where to =
send it's Produce, Fetch, and ShareFetch requests. If it's a share group=
 consumer, it'll send ShareFetch requests to the leader. If it's a norma=
l consumer, it'll send Fetch requests to preferred replica.
2. If the MetadataRequest is older, we also tell the truth. Older client=
s will continue to work, but won't be able to benefit from inter-rack tr=
affic elimination.
2.1. However, as an workaround, we can encode the rack information in th=
e client ID. In this case we "lie" to the consumer by replacing the lead=
er with one of the replicas from the same rack if available.

Best,
Ivan

[1] https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/pages/diffpagesbyversion.action?=
pageId=3D350783976&selectedPageVersions=3D17&selectedPageVersions=3D16

