fujian created KAFKA-20091:
------------------------------

             Summary: Fix inconsistency in time-based retention checks betw=
een remote and local segment deletion logic.=20
                 Key: KAFKA-20091
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20091
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: Tiered-Storage
            Reporter: fujian
            Assignee: fujian


When currentTime- largestTimestamp of segment =3D retentionMs, the behavior=
 is different:
 # Local Segment delete:=C2=A0*Not delete*

org.apache.kafka.storage.internals.log.UnifiedLog#deleteRetentionMsBreached=
Segments:
   boolean delete =3D startMs - segment.largestTimestamp() > retentionMs;

=C2=A0 # Remote segement delete:=C2=A0*Delete*

org.apache.kafka.server.log.remote.storage.RemoteLogManager.RLMExpirationTa=
sk.RemoteLogRetentionHandler#isSegmentBreachedByRetentionTime
shouldDeleteSegment =3D metadata.maxTimestampMs() <=3D retentionTimeData.ge=
t().cleanupUntilMs;

//cleanupUntilMs is time.milliseconds() - retentionMs;
private Optional<RetentionTimeData> buildRetentionTimeData(long retentionMs=
) \{
    long cleanupUntilMs =3D time.milliseconds() - retentionMs;
    return retentionMs > -1 && cleanupUntilMs >=3D 0
            ? Optional.of(new RetentionTimeData(retentionMs, cleanupUntilMs=
))
            : Optional.empty();
}{{}}



