Hey Uladzislau, thanks for the feedback.

On *changelog topics*: since they are regular topics like any others, we
didn=E2=80=99t need to call them out explicitly in the KIP. That said, I=E2=
=80=99m fine
adding a short note there as it doesn=E2=80=99t hurt.

On *non-timestamped state stores*: timestamped stores can also store
records without a timestamp, so there=E2=80=99s no strong reason to include
separate non-timestamped stores, and we may deprecate them at some point.

Bests,
Alieh

