With 4.0 release, we upgraded RocksDB from 7.9 to 9.7 (https://issues.apach=
e.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15443) =E2=80=93 however, we did miss that RocksDB =
introduces a file format version bump from version 5 to version 6 with Rock=
sDB 8.6.

While this does not impact the upgrade path, it does impact the downgrade p=
ath. This limitation is no documented though. =E2=80=93 We should also inve=
stigate `RocksDBConfigSetter` which seems to allow to configure the used fi=
le-format version via `tableconfig.setFormVersion`.

We should also double check system test coverage for upgrade/downgrade path=
 with RocksDB =E2=80=93 ideally we should catch such issue; seems there is =
some testing gap.



