Kamal Chandraprakash resolved KAFKA-20091.
------------------------------------------
    Resolution: Fixed

> Fix inconsistency in time-based retention checks between remote and local=
 segment deletion logic.=20
> -------------------------------------------------------------------------=
-------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-20091
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20091
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Task
>          Components: Tiered-Storage
>            Reporter: fujian
>            Assignee: fujian
>            Priority: Minor
>             Fix For: 4.3.0
>
>
> When currentTime- largestTimestamp of segment =3D retentionMs, the behavi=
or is different:
>  # Local Segment delete:=C2=A0*Not delete*
> org.apache.kafka.storage.internals.log.UnifiedLog#deleteRetentionMsBreach=
edSegments:
> boolean delete =3D startMs - segment.largestTimestamp() > retentionMs;
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A02. Remote segement delete: *Delete*
> org.apache.kafka.server.log.remote.storage.RemoteLogManager.RLMExpiration=
Task.RemoteLogRetentionHandler#isSegmentBreachedByRetentionTime
> shouldDeleteSegment =3D metadata.maxTimestampMs() <=3D retentionTimeData.=
get().cleanupUntilMs;
> //cleanupUntilMs is time.milliseconds() - retentionMs;
> private Optional<RetentionTimeData> buildRetentionTimeData(long retention=
Ms)
> { long cleanupUntilMs =3D time.milliseconds() - retentionMs; return reten=
tionMs > -1 && cleanupUntilMs >=3D 0 ? Optional.of(new RetentionTimeData(re=
tentionMs, cleanupUntilMs)) : Optional.empty(); }
> The PR: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/21352



