Hi everyone,

I=E2=80=99m trying to migrate a test cluster from ZooKeeper to KRaft in-pla=
ce (i.e., not provisioning three new controller-only nodes first and then p=
ointing the existing brokers to them). I hit a problem and would appreciate=
 any pointers.

What I did
- Enabled zookeeper.metadata.migration.enable on each existing broker and s=
et the controller quorum settings so each broker acts as a controller+broke=
r (process.roles=3Dbroker,controller).
- Rolled the three nodes.

Relevant broker configuration (each broker has similar config; example show=
n):

```
process.roles=3Dbroker,controller
[node.id|http://node.id/]=3D7
[broker.id|http://broker.id/]=3D7
zookeeper.metadata.migration.enable=3Dtrue
controller.quorum.voters=3D7@broker1:9093,6@broker2:9093,4@broker3:9093
controller.quorum.bootstrap.servers=3Dbroker1:9093,broker2:9093,broker3:909=
3
zookeeper.connect=3Dzk1:2181,zk2:2181,zk3:2181
controller.listener.names=3DCONTROLLER
[group.initial.rebalance.delay.ms|http://group.initial.rebalance.delay.ms/]=
=3D0
listeners=3DSSL://ip:9092,PLAINTEXT://ip:9192,CONTROLLER://ip:9093
listener.security.protocol.map=3DSSL:SSL,PLAINTEXT:PLAINTEXT,CONTROLLER:PLA=
INTEXT
```

Observed behavior
After rolling restart, the controller logs show the quorum is ready for mig=
ration, but the controller repeatedly logs that no brokers are known to KRa=
ft:

```
[2026-01-27 17:47:15,626] INFO [KRaftMigrationDriver id=3D7] Controller Quo=
rum is ready for Zk to KRaft migration. Now waiting for ZK brokers. (org.ap=
ache.kafka.metadata.migration.KRaftMigrationDriver)
