migration driver repeatedly logs "No brokers are known to KRaft, waiting fo=
r brokers to register." and does not make progress.

My current understanding is as follows:
- Migration from ZooKeeper to KRaft normally involves standing up a separat=
e controller-only KRaft cluster first, then updating the existing brokers t=
o point to that controller cluster (via controller.quorum.bootstrap.servers=
) and enabling zookeeper.metadata.migration.enable.
- Performing an in-place migration (having the existing brokers also act as=
 controllers) seems risky because controller quorum elections require a maj=
ority of controller nodes. For example, with topics having replication.fact=
or=3D2, you may need to restart two brokers to form the new controller quor=
um, which would make RF=3D2 topics unavailable during the migration.
